-- A BREACH BY a list as an operand of a RAND or ROR, wherever the party type
-- is known by the time the list is read: from the GIVETH, which reaches both
-- operands, or from a PARTY operand checked before it. Each list names one
-- party per element. Before this branch ported unstable's
-- checkRegulativeBinOp, each of these was refused at the BREACH
-- (check/breach-by-list-needs-party-type). Each answer under l4 run equals
-- unstable's. (The adversarial pass of 2026-11-20: F3, F3b, BL-1, BL-4.)

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob, Carol, Dave
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF deliver, notify, exercise, noop
DECLARE Step IS ONE OF handover, idle

-- 1. The second operand, under a GIVETH, after an operand that names nobody.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`second operand of an ROR` MEANS
    (FULFILLED) ROR (BREACH BY LIST Alice, Bob BECAUSE "x")

#TRACE `second operand of an ROR` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Dave DOES exercise AT 20

-- 2. The same as the second operand of a RAND.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`second operand of a RAND` MEANS
    (FULFILLED) RAND (BREACH BY LIST Alice, Bob BECAUSE "x")

#TRACE `second operand of a RAND` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Dave DOES exercise AT 20

-- 3. No GIVETH: the first operand of the RIGHT operand, after a PARTY operand
--    that fixes the party type.
`first operand of the right operand` MEANS
    (PARTY Dave MUST notify WITHIN 4)
    RAND
    ((BREACH BY LIST Alice, Bob BECAUSE "x") RAND (PARTY Carol MUST deliver WITHIN 3))

#TRACE `first operand of the right operand` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Dave DOES exercise AT 20

-- 4. No GIVETH: the first operand of a RAND under a LEST, whose PARTY line
--    fixes the party type.
`first operand under a LEST` MEANS
    PARTY Alice MUST deliver WITHIN 5
    LEST ((BREACH BY LIST Alice, Bob) RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 3))

#TRACE `first operand under a LEST` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES noop AT 20

-- 5. No GIVETH, a party whose value is a list, and one BY naming it: the
--    PARTY line fixes the party type as the list's type, so the list is ONE
--    party.
`a list-valued party under a LEST` MEANS
    PARTY (LIST "a") MUST handover WITHIN 5
    LEST (FULFILLED RAND (BREACH BY (LIST "a")))

#TRACE `a list-valued party under a LEST` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY (LIST "a") DOES idle AT 20
